    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Here's what I think. The coughing at meals after a stroke, with the wet voice, suggests swallowing difficulty after the stroke.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:37",
      "end_timestamp": "03:49",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Very. I'm also concerned that some food or drink may go into the lungs, so I can't rule out that it's already getting there.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:55",
      "end_timestamp": "04:10",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It can be, which is why I'd like to arrange a swallowing assessment with a speech therapist, soon.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:16",
      "end_timestamp": "04:27",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
